<ServicePage title="RubberBond EPDM Flat Roofing Yorkshire | WW Roofing" description="Leeds-based RubberBond FleeceBack EPDM installation across Yorkshire and beyond. Flat roof replacement, refurbishment and new builds, assessed for your property." kicker="Our specialism / RubberBond FleeceBack EPDM" heading="A flat roof built around your property." intro="Specialist rubber roofing for homes and larger buildings across Yorkshire and beyond. We consider the whole construction, from the deck beneath it to the way rainwater leaves it.">
<section class="section"><div class="wrap content-grid"><div class="editorial"><h2>Why we install RubberBond</h2><p>RubberBond FleeceBack EPDM combines a flexible synthetic rubber membrane with a polyester backing. The fleece helps protect against punctures, while EPDM offers resistance to UV exposure and ozone. It is a roofing system with its own adhesives, seams and detailing components.</p><p>Wide sheets can reduce the number of joints across a roof. Installation uses cold-applied bonding and seam detailing, without torch-on membrane application. Roof shape, access and weather still influence the programme.</p><h2>Replacement, refurbishment or new build?</h2><p>We inspect the condition of the covering and deck, moisture, falls and drainage before recommending a build-up. Some sound existing roofs may be suitable for an overlay. Others need stripping and repairs before new waterproofing can be installed.</p><p>Insulation is considered alongside vapour control and condensation risk. Tapered insulation can help form drainage falls when appropriate. Outlets, upstands, rooflights and connections to neighbouring roofs need as much attention as the main surface.</p><h2>What the installation involves</h2><ol><li><strong>Assess:</strong> inspect the roof and understand the problem or proposed design.</li><li><strong>Specify:</strong> agree preparation, insulation, drainage and waterproofing details.</li><li><strong>Install:</strong> prepare the substrate, fit the specified layers, bond the membrane and complete junctions.</li><li><strong>Handover:</strong> explain care requirements and applicable warranty arrangements.</li></ol><h2>Specialist installation, with technical support</h2><p>WW Roofing & Building is your roofing contractor. As a Flex-R Specialist Registered Installer (SRI), we have product-specific training and access to technical guidance from the system supplier. <a href="/about/#specialist-installer">Learn about the installer relationship</a>.</p><h2>Service life and warranties</h2><p>The BBA certificate linked from Flex-R’s downloads, 22/6056 Product Sheet 3, describes at least 35 years’ service life under normal service conditions, subject to its installation, use and maintenance provisions. That assessment is not a guarantee for an individual roof.</p><p>Warranty availability, duration, cover and inspection requirements depend on the specified project and written terms offered. We establish the applicable arrangements for your quote. Product certification concerns the roofing system; it is not accreditation of WW or a blanket statement that every roof build-up complies.</p><p><a href="https://flex-r.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/07/RubberBond-FleeceBack-BBA-2022-6056ps3i1.pdf">Read the BBA document supplied by Flex-R (PDF)</a> · <a href="https://flex-r.co.uk/audience/sri-contractors/">Flex-R system and installer information</a></p></div><aside class="aside-panel"><img src="/images/mount-st-mary-2.webp" alt="WW’s completed RubberBond flat roof at Mount St Mary" width="1536" height="866" loading="lazy"/><h2>One system. Different buildings.</h2><p>Extensions, dormers and garages; new homes, apartment blocks, schools and commercial buildings. Suitability is assessed for each roof.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sectors/residential/">For homeowners ↗</a><br/><a class="text-link" href="/sectors/commercial/">For commercial projects ↗</a><h2 style="margin-top:35px">Have a leaking flat roof?</h2><p>Tell us where you see the problem, what the roof covers and your postcode. Photos taken safely from ground level can help.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Talk to WW ↗</a></aside></div></section>
<section class="other-band"><div class="wrap editorial faq-list"><h2>Flat roofing questions</h2><details><summary>Can you cover my existing felt roof?</summary><p>Possibly. An overlay needs a suitable, sound and dry construction. We assess adhesion, moisture, deck condition and details before deciding whether to retain or remove it.</p></details><details><summary>Will a new membrane solve standing water?</summary><p>A membrane alone does not create drainage falls. We assess outlets and roof geometry and discuss changes to the build-up where needed.</p></details><details><summary>Can I walk on the finished roof?</summary><p>Maintenance access and regular use are different requirements. Tell us how the roof will be used so that suitable protection or a separate terrace finish can be considered.</p></details><details><summary>How much will it cost?</summary><p>Area, condition, access, insulation and junction details all affect the work. Send your postcode and project details so we can arrange the next step towards a quote.</p></details></div></section><FlatProject/>
